  "runtime_invariants": [
    "Authenticate and authorize the exact project before any lookup, count, cursor or projection; no owner-token fallback for engines or employees.",
    "Every entity/reference scope must equal the request project. Task response task_id and task.entity.id must equal the requested task_id; recheck dependencies/artifacts/review attempts/check artifacts individually.",
    "Cursor is opaque, integrity protected, expiring and bound to authenticated principal, credential identity, project, operation, task, section, limit, query and snapshot. No caller identity/scope is trusted from cursor plaintext.",
    "Each response is assembled from one consistent read snapshot. Reject a changed continuation snapshot with 409 snapshot_changed and no partial records; reject invalid/expired/restarted-server cursors with 409 continuation_invalid.",
    "Page returned_count equals array length and never exceeds limit. No total counts. Truncation always supplies continuation for remaining authorized rows; oversized mandatory headers fail 413 rather than silently dropping fields.",
    "Only approved logical repository identities and relative boundaries are projected; omit no required scope/provenance field and expose no host path, storage_key, registry/token, raw SQL row or execution authority.",
    "Artifact source origin and actual references are preserved. Controller exports never invent task, attempt, employee, machine or generation. Include a task artifact only through an existing checked task association.",
    "Review reads retrieve sealed stored receipts only; no ready_for_owner/evaluate/collect mutation and no acceptance inference. Missing mandate/knowledge/canonical-dossier capabilities remain unavailable.",
    "Reading pages must not create tasks, attempts, approvals, reservations, readiness receipts, effects or Store records."
  ],
